   "question": "The claim under test holds that Er and Ce are incorporated into the co-doped particles, with each element sitting in the stated oxidation state and Ce present as a mixed-valence surface species. Looking at the two XPS panels (F6c, F6d) cited as evidence for this, does the data actually confirm the labeled peak assignments for each element, and why or why not?",
   "answer_key": "No. Panel F6c, the region where a Ce mixed-valence signal is expected, is noise with no resolved peaks at the marked positions, and in panel F6d the fitted envelope for the Er signal sits well above the noisy underlying data, so the fit is not supported by the actual signal (o21).",
   "answer_scope": "full",
